56"><span class="enc-name">Tushratta</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Tushratta was a king of the Mitanni Empire in the fourteenth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tuskahoma-oklahoma"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tuskahoma-oklahoma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tuskahoma, Oklahoma</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tuskahoma is a small community in Pushmataha County, south-eastern Oklahoma, United States.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tutuila"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tutuila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tutuila</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tutuila is the largest and most populous island of American Samoa, in the South Pacific.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tutul-xiu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tutul-xiu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tutul Xiu</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tutul Xiu were a Maya ruling lineage of northern Yucatán, associated with Uxmal and, after the fall of Mayapán in the mid-15th century, with the town of Maní.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/tutush-i"><span class="enc-name">Tutush I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Tutush I was a Seljuk prince, brother of Sultan Malik-Shah I, who founded the Seljuk Sultanate of Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tuul-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tuul-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tuul River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tuul is